From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MC-xiaonan <2106104879@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:42:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Guard Commands.performCommand against off-global-thread
 invocation

AsyncCatcher.catchOp only rejects non-tick-thread callers (bare
isTickThread(), true for any tick thread). Command execution has
unbounded cross-region side effects and no region ownership of its
own, so once region worker threads exist it must stay pinned to the
single global tick thread. Add an explicit isGlobalTickThread()
check. No RegionWorkerThread exists yet, so this is zero behavior
change today.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/commands/Commands.java b/net/minecraft/commands/Commands.java
index c4396509584011a5bbc171510478e8e62ce44d94..e14723a0260b6818717ec18159f204c27eeba584 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/commands/Commands.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/commands/Commands.java
@@ -368,6 +368,16 @@ public class Commands {
 
     public void performCommand(final ParseResults<CommandSourceStack> command, final String commandString, final boolean throwCommandError) {
         org.spigotmc.AsyncCatcher.catchOp("Cannot perform command async");
+        // LcsXNMC start - region threading: command execution can have unbounded cross-region side
+        // effects (e.g. /tp, /kill @e) and has no region ownership of its own, so it must stay pinned
+        // to the single global tick thread even once region worker threads exist. AsyncCatcher.catchOp()
+        // above only rejects non-tick-thread callers (it uses the bare, over-permissive isTickThread()
+        // check shared by call sites that *do* want to allow any region worker), so it alone would not
+        // catch a region worker (e.g. one ticking a command block) calling in here directly.
+        if (!ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.TickThread.isGlobalTickThread()) {
+            throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot perform command \"" + commandString + "\" off the global tick thread");
+        }
+        // LcsXNMC end - region threading
         // Paper end
         CommandSourceStack sender = command.getContext().getSource();
         Profiler.get().push(() -> "/" + commandString);
